{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-L19-phone-shop-2-01","date":"2026-11-21","lens":"19","surface":"phone","area":"phone/shop-2","refs":["F-phone-433","FN-L19-phone-lib-core-01"],"severity":"S4","title":"Once MettleUp Plus is on, a gym member whose plan ended can keep the paid extras by setting the phone's date back","what":"The gym tells the app the member's plan end date, and the app then decides on its own whether the 7 days after the end are over, using the phone's own date. Setting the phone's date back, or never letting the app go online again, keeps the paid extras open. Any doubt also opens everything. The switch for this is off today.","expected":"The 'is the plan over' answer should come from the server's date when online, and an app that has not reached the server for a long time should stop trusting its kept end date.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/plan/memberPlanStore.ts:69-76","apps/mobile/src/plan/memberPlanStore.ts:90-93","apps/mobile/src/shop/gymApi.ts:727-735"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"plus-end-judged-by-phone-clock","who":"members","how_often":"only when someone tries","fix_line":"Check the plan end against the server's date, not the phone's","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
